course: dictionary
lesson: 9698
title: A very serious word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Suicide is a very serious word. It means deliberately ending your own life. Because it is so serious, people use careful, gentle words when they talk about it.
explain: «Took his own life» means killed himself. It is the gentle way to speak of suicide, and it is the way newspapers and teachers often choose to say it.
explain: The word can also be used in a figurative sense, for a choice that badly harms your own chances, as in «career suicide», which means ruining your own work or future. This is a different, everyday use, but it still shows how strong the word is.
explain: If you ever feel like hurting yourself or ending your life, do not carry that feeling alone. Tell a trusted adult straight away. Help lines are always there for you, and reaching out is brave.
fact: Suicide means deliberately ending your own life.
fact: The gentle way to say it is «took his own life», which means killed himself.
fact: «Die by suicide» is the preferred phrase, and «suicide prevention» means work done to stop people taking their own lives.
fact: In a figurative sense, «career suicide» means a choice that badly harms your own work chances.
fact: If you feel like hurting yourself, tell a trusted adult. Help lines are always there for you.
exercise: What does suicide mean? | Losing a game very badly | Being very good at a sport | A kind of bird that cannot fly | *The act of deliberately ending your own life
exercise: Which gentle phrase means the same as suicide? | Ran away from home | *Took his own life | Fell fast asleep | Went on holiday
exercise: Mr Shah says quitting rudely would be «career suicide». What does suicide mean here? | A very fast way to travel | A brand new job | *A choice that would badly harm your own work chances | A kind goodbye card
test: If someone feels like hurting themselves, what should you do? | Wait and see if it passes | Keep it a secret | Laugh about it with friends | *Tell a trusted adult straight away
test: What is true about help lines? | They are a waste of time | *Help is always there for you if you reach out | They are only open for one hour a day | Only grown-up doctors can use them
exam: Which phrase is the preferred, careful way to talk about suicide? | A sad story | A dramatic ending | *Die by suicide | A quick way out
